  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Thundercat Technology has $169M in federal contract obligations for FY2027 to date. Thundercat Technology received 85 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $2M. Thundercat Technology's obligations are down 85.5% year over year. Thundercat Technology's obligation history shows growth through FY26, including $680M in FY22, $854M in FY23, $807M in FY24, $916M in FY25, and $1.2B in FY26, before the current-year total of $169M. Thundercat Technology's largest buying agency for FY2027 to date is the Department of Veterans Affairs with $150M. Thundercat Technology's next-largest buying agencies are the National Aeronautics and Space Administration with $8.1M and the Department of Agriculture with $5.6M. Thundercat Technology's top NAICS market for FY2027 to date is Other Computer Related Services with $169M, while Software Publishers shows $0 in obligations this year. The current-year totals are partial, and award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables are total contract values rather than obligations.",
    "sections": [
